  "screen.cutscene": "Cutscene",
  "cutscene.line": "{name}: {text}",
  "cutscene.ember.name": "Ember",
  "cutscene.choice": "{n}: {text}",
  "cutscene.notes.ghast1.01": "It’s been a while, hasn’t it? I pause, trying to recall how EXODUS is laid out.",
  "cutscene.notes.ghast1.02": "It comes back in pieces. The screen is a row of groups. Tab steps forward through them, Shift and Tab steps back.",
  "cutscene.notes.ghast1.03": "The task first. What they want, a checklist that fills itself in as I deliver, and Show Goal when I need the whole brief.",
  "cutscene.notes.ghast1.04": "Then my windows. Every EXA I’ve written, every file in the current network. Enter on an EXA and I’m inside its code.",
  "cutscene.notes.ghast1.05": "Then the hosts. One row each, with whoever is standing in it.",
  "cutscene.notes.ghast1.06": "Then its links. Enter on a link and I’m through it, looking at the other side.",
  "cutscene.notes.ghast1.07": "Its files and its hardware registers work the same way. Enter on a file and every value in it is read to me.",
  "cutscene.notes.ghast1.08": "Then the code itself. I type. F2 steps one cycle and tells me what each EXA is about to do.",
  "cutscene.notes.ghast1.09": "Outside the code, X, T, F or M reads that register of the last EXA I touched.",
  "cutscene.notes.ghast1.10": "After the code, the scores. Then the simulation: run, fast, pause, reset. The old function keys still do the same.",
  "cutscene.notes.ghast1.11": "Then the logs, once something has run. I don’t remember what they keep. I do remember Control and the arrows, jumping cycle to cycle.",
  "cutscene.notes.ghast1.12": "The solution sits at the very end. Name it, or make another EXA.",
  "cutscene.notes.ghast1.13": "Escape does what it always did. Reset a run, or leave.",
  "cutscene.notes.ghast1.14": "Muscle memory. One of the few things the phage hasn’t taken yet.",

